        "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "We use the cosecant-cotangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x={csc}^{2}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-0-(-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
